# GitHub Actions: ordinary public release.
# Repository -> Actions -> workflow below -> Run workflow.
# Push the code first. Select the same branch for every run; keep it unchanged.
# Wait for each run to succeed before continuing. Leave other inputs at defaults.

1. Maintain base SDK (sdk-base.yml)                         [optional]
   Run with platform=linux, then with platform=windows.
   Keep source=auto and publish=true.
   Skip either run if its current dependency recipe is already in base.

2. Focused checks and full native regression (ci.yml)
   devfast=false (unchecked).

3. Application checks with the base SDK (sdk.yml)
   devfast=false (unchecked).

4. Manual portable release (release.yml)
   experiment=false (uncheck it); publish=true (checked).
   Leave version blank to use the application version plus a timestamp.
   Copy the new release tag from the run summary.

5. Certify published release (certify.yml)
   release_tag=the new tag from step 4; devfast=false (unchecked).

# Done: the certified ordinary release becomes Latest, with public Linux/Windows
# binaries, Linux packages and retained build dependencies. Review any warnings
# in its certification report; record the tag, run IDs and limits in docs/validation.md.
# First-time signing setup and details: docs/releases.md
